From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: edk2-cix <edk2-cix@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 23:48:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Platform/CIX/Sky1: PlatformSetupVariableInitDxe: fix stack
 overrun

GetVariable() returns EFI_BUFFER_TOO_SMALL and the stored size when the
variable is larger than the current structure (for example after
flashing an older firmware).  Both init paths then called ZeroMem() with
that size on a stack buffer of sizeof (structure), overrunning the stack
before the variable was rewritten.  Clear the structure with its own size.

From Neol00/edk2-cix-unlocked V2.4.
---
 .../PlatformSetupVariableInitDxe.c                            | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Platform/CIX/Sky1/Drivers/PlatformSetupVariableInitDxe/PlatformSetupVariableInitDxe.c b/Platform/CIX/Sky1/Drivers/PlatformSetupVariableInitDxe/PlatformSetupVariableInitDxe.c
index 731ea28c..5da6ec06 100644
--- a/Platform/CIX/Sky1/Drivers/PlatformSetupVariableInitDxe/PlatformSetupVariableInitDxe.c
+++ b/Platform/CIX/Sky1/Drivers/PlatformSetupVariableInitDxe/PlatformSetupVariableInitDxe.c
@@ -553,7 +553,7 @@ PlatformSetupVariableInit (
     //
     // Variable does not exist yet - create it
     //
-    ZeroMem (&PlatformSetupVar, VarSize);
+    ZeroMem (&PlatformSetupVar, sizeof (PlatformSetupVar));
     ConstructSetupVariable (&PlatformSetupVar);
 
     Status = gRT->SetVariable (
@@ -592,7 +592,7 @@ NetworkStackVariableInit (
                   &NetworkStack
                   );
   if (EFI_ERROR (Status)) {
-    ZeroMem (&NetworkStack, VarSize);
+    ZeroMem (&NetworkStack, sizeof (NetworkStack));
     //
     // Variable does not exist yet - create it
     //
